      "message": "Is there a pre-existing bug (also in the non-Rust path) when this gets pulled out in [SkiaImageDecoderBase::OnSetData](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/platform/image-decoders/skia/skia_image_decoder_base.cc;l\u003d101;drc\u003d8b3cdb2cec78482a46337fc2a53db52974a2920a). That seems to just copy the `skcms_ICCProfile` object directly into the `blink::ColorProfile`, with all of the pointers still dangling.\n\nIf that\u0027s the case, then we probably need to find a solution that fixes that as well. I might be inclined to create a bigger \"color profile object\" that includes the ICC profile, any \"guts\" needed for its pointers, and the HDR metadata all together. But maybe there\u0027s a better solution out there.",
